Track 2: The Brakeman's Confession
- Story & Context: Over a cup of bitter instant coffee in the grimy breakroom of the Ferroviária terminal, old Eduardo, the veteran brakeman, admitted he'd been slipping little messages—poems—into the empty conductors’ boxes for years, his quiet rebellion against the endless, repetitive grind of the night runs, a secret longing whispered only to the steel and the dark, finding its beat in the train's own rhythm: "This carriage, it carries more than just cargo, doesn't it?"
